  "details": "Observed in versions: \n2020.10.28.15.57 and 2020.09.25.00.08\nDescription of bug: \nThe 'VRChat/Mobile/Lightmapped' shader interacts with Unity's lightmapper in an unexpected way. Specifically, indirect lighting is calculated incorrectly. \nThe expected behaviour is that light bouncing off a material will lose some energy and be tinted by the material's colour. It seems like VRChat's Lightmapped shader is always treated like a perfectly white surface, ignoring the texture colour.\nI work around this issue by setting all my world materials to Unity's Standard shader before baking. Then I switch them all to VRChat's Lightmapped shader. However, this is inconvenient and I also worry that less experienced creators may either not notice this issue or may not realise that it can be avoided and therefore have the quality of their work undermined by boring monochromatic lighting.\nI've included some example screenshots from a test world as well as screenshots of my lighting settings.",
